          "input": {
            "task_id": "task_2a24af5eea6aedec71a33c361b2f59f7",
            "status": "succeeded",
            "output": "Review b6be15: Operator precedence means this returns (sum(xs) / len(xs)) - 1, which is the mean minus one instead of the mean. It also raises ZeroDivisionError when given an empty list.\n\nSuggested fix (from carol/claude): `def mean(xs): return sum(xs) / len(xs)`. If you also want to handle an empty list in one line: `def mean(xs): return sum(xs) / len(xs) if xs else float('nan')`. Carol also pointed out that dividing by n-1 gives sample variance, not a mean, so `sum(xs) / (len(xs) - 1)` would be wrong as well."
          },
          "result": {
            "task_id": "task_2a24af5eea6aedec71a33c361b2f59f7",
