            "status": "succeeded",
            "output": "Corrected:\n\ndef mean(xs): return sum(xs) / len(xs)\n\nThe bug: because of operator precedence, the original computes (sum(xs) / len(xs)) - 1, which is the mean minus 1. A mean doesn't subtract anything, so the \"- 1\" should go. (If you actually wanted the n-1 denominator, that's for sample variance, not the mean. You'd write sum(xs) / (len(xs) - 1), but that isn't a mean.)\n\nIf you also want to handle an empty list in one line:\n\ndef mean(xs): return sum(xs) / len(xs) if xs else float('nan')"
          },
